
1️⃣ Start the Lab
Prepare the environment.
lab start cli-review
________________________________________
2️⃣ Login as Developer
Connect to the cluster.
oc login -u developer -p developer https://api.ocp4.example.com:6443
Create a project (namespace):
oc new-project cli-review
Project = namespace used for your resources
________________________________________
3️⃣ Get Cluster Version
Shows OpenShift + Kubernetes versions.
oc version
Example output:
Client Version: 4.18.6
Kubernetes Version: v1.31.6
Important for:
•	compatibility
•	debugging
•	upgrades
________________________________________
4️⃣ List Supported API Versions
oc api-versions
Example:
apps/v1
apiserver.openshift.io/v1
oauth.openshift.io/v1
This shows all APIs supported by the cluster.
________________________________________
5️⃣ View Kubernetes Object Fields
Example: security context of pods
oc explain pod.spec.securityContext
This command:
•	explains Kubernetes objects
•	shows fields
•	used for YAML creation
Example structure:
pod
 └─ spec
     └─ securityContext
________________________________________
6️⃣ Login as Admin
Admin has full cluster permissions.
oc login -u admin -p redhatocp https://api.ocp4.example.com:6443
________________________________________
7️⃣ List Cluster Operators
Cluster operators manage core components.
oc get clusteroperators
Example:
authentication
console
dns
etcd
kube-apiserver
Healthy operator:
AVAILABLE=True
PROGRESSING=False
DEGRADED=False
________________________________________
8️⃣ List Namespaced Resources
Shows resources that exist inside namespaces.
oc api-resources --namespaced
Example:
Resource	Shortname
pods	po
configmaps	cm
services	svc
pvc	persistentvolumeclaims
These resources belong to projects/namespaces.
________________________________________
9️⃣ List Core API Group Resources
Core API group = no group name ("")
oc api-resources --api-group ''
Examples:
pods
nodes
namespaces
configmaps
events
These are basic Kubernetes resources.
________________________________________
🔟 List Resources from OAuth API Group
oc api-resources --api-group oauth.openshift.io
Example:
oauthaccesstokens
oauthauthorizationtokens
oauthclients
These resources manage authentication and login tokens.
________________________________________
1️⃣1️⃣ View Cluster Events
Events help diagnose problems.
oc get events -n openshift-kube-controller-manager
Examples:
LeaderElection
Pulled
Started
Events show:
•	pod startup
•	scheduling
•	errors
•	leader election
________________________________________
1️⃣2️⃣ Check Pod Conditions Using jq
Retrieve pod status conditions.
oc get pods etcd-master01 -n openshift-etcd -o json | jq .status.conditions
Example output:
Initialized
Ready
ContainersReady
PodScheduled
Meaning:
Condition	Meaning
Initialized	Pod initialized
Ready	Pod ready for traffic
ContainersReady	containers running
PodScheduled	assigned to node
________________________________________
1️⃣3️⃣ View Container Resource Usage
Check CPU + memory per container.
oc adm top pods etcd-master01 -n openshift-etcd --containers
Example:
etcd            101m   323Mi
etcd-metrics      8m    32Mi
Useful for:
•	performance monitoring
•	troubleshooting
________________________________________
1️⃣4️⃣ Get Allocatable Pods Using JSONPath
oc get node master01 -o jsonpath='{.status.allocatable.pods}'
Example:
250
Meaning:
Node can run 250 pods maximum.
________________________________________
1️⃣5️⃣ View Cluster Pod Resource Usage
oc adm top pods -A --sum
Options:
Option	Meaning
-A	all namespaces
--sum	total resource usage
Example total:
CPU: 386m
Memory: 11929Mi
________________________________________
1️⃣6️⃣ Check Node Resource Usage
oc adm top node
Example:
CPU: 1199m (15%)
Memory: 12555Mi (66%)
Used for node capacity monitoring.
________________________________________
1️⃣7️⃣ Check Node CPU Capacity
oc get node master01 -o jsonpath='Allocatable: {.status.allocatable.cpu}{"\n"}Capacity: {.status.capacity.cpu}'
Example:
Allocatable: 7500m
Capacity: 8
Meaning:
Value	Meaning
Capacity	total CPU
Allocatable	CPU available for pods
________________________________________
1️⃣8️⃣ Collect Cluster Debug Information
Run:
oc adm must-gather --dest-dir /home/student/DO180/labs/cli-review/debugging
This collects:
•	cluster logs
•	configurations
•	operator states
•	events
Used for Red Hat support cases.
________________________________________
1️⃣9️⃣ Inspect Specific Operator
Example:
oc adm inspect clusteroperator kube-apiserver \
--dest-dir /home/student/DO180/labs/cli-review/inspect \
--since 5m
Options:
Option	Meaning
--dest-dir	output directory
--since	collect recent logs
________________________________________
2️⃣0️⃣ Grade the Lab
Check answers.
lab grade cli-review
Fix errors if any.
________________________________________
2️⃣1️⃣ Finish Lab
Clean up resources.
lab finish cli-review
